                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6c9027c3-c3b0-4d45-8777-7d39c9616026",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f279b6a-24bb-3411-96d4-0eaec47fba65",
                        "source_sense_id": "8891929b-bf0f-31ef-967e-6192835b2e6b",
                        "target_lang_word": "hooligan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hooligan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d669b64-c14a-349a-b988-0127ce798e77",
                                        "entry_id": "d3dd53e3-9545-3516-8061-bbbb85473104",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A young person who causes trouble or violence, typically as a member of a gang or other group."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "attributive",
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91b92200-d663-436a-ada6-6808b4908191",
                                                "sense_id": "9d669b64-c14a-349a-b988-0127ce798e77",
                                                "text": "She also heard boys from other classes behind her talking: “So, Teacher Tang is a female hooligan.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fa0a721-c3a5-4a38-a979-ce76699f9830",
                                                "sense_id": "9d669b64-c14a-349a-b988-0127ce798e77",
                                                "text": "And I was in danger of turning into a right little hooligan if left to my wayward ways."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86acfce9-4783-4ab1-96de-abc6a14f61fa",
                                                "sense_id": "9d669b64-c14a-349a-b988-0127ce798e77",
                                                "text": "“You are hooligan, you try to make trouble.” Sam paused, then continued. “Ah ha ha ha, I am right, I see it in your eyes. A hooligan!”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "45fed399-ecfc-339f-828c-6e6bfeece0cf",
                                        "entry_id": "d3dd53e3-9545-3516-8061-bbbb85473104",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of football hooligan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d91e2533-e4c9-4090-be88-64442d0daf3b",
                                                "sense_id": "45fed399-ecfc-339f-828c-6e6bfeece0cf",
                                                "text": "These excursions abroad confirm that displacement has actually been a feature of the development of hooligan conflicts for some time, but an important wider point is that domestic hooligan displacement also seems to be a much more central issue today, as policing and other control strategies (segregation, seating, stewarding and CCTV in and around the larger English football grounds) have become more comprehensive, and especially as sentences for hooliganism have become much more forbidding."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb34a5ae-fe88-3734-8281-37dd35ccae69",
                                        "entry_id": "d3dd53e3-9545-3516-8061-bbbb85473104",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of the United States Coast Guard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b954f8f9-7a64-40d8-a567-d7c7cc53cf4a",
                                                "sense_id": "cb34a5ae-fe88-3734-8281-37dd35ccae69",
                                                "text": "Many professional Navy and Coast Guard men were inclined to scoff. What kind of Navy was this, and what did they think they were up to, anyway? This bunch of hooligans wouldn't be any good to anyone; wouldn't be worth the powder to blow 'em to hell. Hooligan's Navy."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60d0606d-b660-4194-b244-27fb0559f18d",
                                                "sense_id": "cb34a5ae-fe88-3734-8281-37dd35ccae69",
                                                "text": "It often seemed to Al that the entire Coast Guard was a little embarrassed about being Coast Guardsmen—except maybe the cocky bearded men off the convoy cutters, who needed to apologize to no man because of any lack of battle stars. But in general, Army and Navy guys looked down on Hooligans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf7eef92-3c89-4e80-8431-26534b588d44",
                                                "sense_id": "cb34a5ae-fe88-3734-8281-37dd35ccae69",
                                                "text": "I frequently notice that the hooligans (a respectful reference to the U.S. Coast Guard) are a hard act to follow."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "89a57fe9-7315-47b8-92ce-4489878af48b",
                                                "sense_id": "cb34a5ae-fe88-3734-8281-37dd35ccae69",
                                                "text": "Navy crew along the rail shouted smart-ass remarks and jeered at the hooligan doing his job."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hooligan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "358851e7-28ea-36d2-864c-565ca07e31ea",
                                        "entry_id": "3e0bf163-bda9-399f-ac9e-a5c000e9725e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To act as a hooligan (sense 1)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b5405d6-98f7-3046-9aa2-fabb53ea1b64",
                                        "entry_id": "3e0bf163-bda9-399f-ac9e-a5c000e9725e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To treat (a person) roughly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hooligan",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7480f55f-56ec-3f1a-bc35-a38493ca60d2",
                                        "entry_id": "87422f91-3e69-33a6-8b3c-2a45794ee91d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of fish, an anadromous smelt, Thaleichthys pacificus, found in the North Pacific."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "053fee64-8fc5-4b9e-ac41-1cdc13172e52",
                                                "sense_id": "7480f55f-56ec-3f1a-bc35-a38493ca60d2",
                                                "text": "One year there was a strong wind. We couldn’t catch herring, but they were there. We caught lots of hooligans (smelt) and got through the year on those."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df8b63c2-6d9d-4831-adbd-29288a12bf32",
                                                "sense_id": "7480f55f-56ec-3f1a-bc35-a38493ca60d2",
                                                "text": "Haines and Klukwan hooligan harvesters reported that they exchanged hooligan products primarily for other food items, especially those unavailable in the Chilkat and Chilkoot area or those which were inaccessible to the harvester for various reasons. Respondents reported that virtually any wild food might be obtained for hooligan oil."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "abb0d09c-f7d1-42e7-b9dc-2ffbcc8dc79a",
                                                "sense_id": "7480f55f-56ec-3f1a-bc35-a38493ca60d2",
                                                "text": "Low-gradient, clear water streams on the western side of Portage Pass provide spawning and rearing habitat for red salmon, silver salmon, pink salmon, chum salmon, hooligan (smelt), and Dolly Varden (U.S. Bureau of Land Management 1977b)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c1bcc5d5-41d2-46fd-8b89-594376c3d608",
                                                "sense_id": "7480f55f-56ec-3f1a-bc35-a38493ca60d2",
                                                "text": "Hooligan (smelt) are often spotted from the point as they come in with the tide."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "80675d08-cfbf-49ec-85f2-d40985b3bf0f",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f279b6a-24bb-3411-96d4-0eaec47fba65",
                        "source_sense_id": "8891929b-bf0f-31ef-967e-6192835b2e6b",
                        "target_lang_word": "scamp",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "scamp",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "da8bab4b-6e61-35e1-9f00-8262d2ec8d0e",
                                        "entry_id": "04c560c5-70d9-3430-88bd-0ef75a4b223a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rascal, swindler, or rogue; a ne'er-do-well."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af1e55ee-0f9e-470f-a879-c01e0042d3bd",
                                                "sense_id": "da8bab4b-6e61-35e1-9f00-8262d2ec8d0e",
                                                "text": "\"He is a scamp, he is and it isn't difficult to find his tracks and signs of his reckless shooting, for he can never wait, like other folks, till the birds have had a good start at their play.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70f8931c-5aed-39df-81ef-280e784ff970",
                                        "entry_id": "04c560c5-70d9-3430-88bd-0ef75a4b223a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mischievous person, especially a playful, impish youngster."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b951088-39bd-459a-bf3d-2069db7a924b",
                                                "sense_id": "70f8931c-5aed-39df-81ef-280e784ff970",
                                                "text": "My nephew is a little scamp who likes to leave lighted firecrackers under the lawnchairs of his dozing elders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d2951492-7a74-43f7-b277-d4fc6b5dffeb",
                                                "sense_id": "70f8931c-5aed-39df-81ef-280e784ff970",
                                                "text": "While walking home from the bar, he was set upon by a bunch of scamps who stole his hat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fb2b9ef-f289-4fbd-9544-3fb4f32ecd2f",
                                                "sense_id": "70f8931c-5aed-39df-81ef-280e784ff970",
                                                "text": "Prince Harry idolized Diana more and understood her less. He would always be her baby, a scamp who was “thick” at his lessons and “naughty, just like me.” His emotions, like hers, were always simmering near the surface."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scamp",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e01ff16-ccda-3044-9739-184271af4260",
                                        "entry_id": "c2c71d9c-2049-392d-b1b8-aaf9ab20b69d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To skimp; to do something in a skimpy or slipshod fashion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2b0f2e8-6e41-4b20-9a6e-11e6f19a0802",
                                                "sense_id": "4e01ff16-ccda-3044-9739-184271af4260",
                                                "text": "1884, Samuel Smiles, Men of Invention and Industry\nHis work was always first-rate. There was no scamping about it. Everything that he did was thoroughly good and honest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf515cfe-b126-4220-85b9-12ffddc6d080",
                                                "sense_id": "4e01ff16-ccda-3044-9739-184271af4260",
                                                "text": "“They know our boats will stand up to their work,” said Willison, “and that counts for a good deal. A low estimate from us doesn't mean scamped work, but just for that we want to keep the yard busy over a slack time.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "scamp",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9340b211-1599-35a7-b4c0-4f9283f2f22d",
                                        "entry_id": "189d1af4-b741-3dd0-8874-42cc41755ed5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A preliminary design sketch."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50087d7d-0058-41af-b93b-294972a0da2d",
                                                "sense_id": "9340b211-1599-35a7-b4c0-4f9283f2f22d",
                                                "text": "It did not matter that the scamp (simple illustrative line-drawing) it contained could have been done in the pub the night before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e0709b93-ff78-4b51-84ed-6c0b5bfd84e6",
                                                "sense_id": "9340b211-1599-35a7-b4c0-4f9283f2f22d",
                                                "text": "From the scamps, the creative idea can be developed more fully into a proposal for an actual ad. This needs to be clear enough to present to the client."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f4c61578-c95e-47cb-a986-97c36ec5b835",
                        "source_entry_id": "1f279b6a-24bb-3411-96d4-0eaec47fba65",
                        "source_sense_id": "8891929b-bf0f-31ef-967e-6192835b2e6b",
                        "target_lang_word": "Flegel",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Flegel",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e78ee83-3170-385b-855c-f7d285caa0a5",
                                        "entry_id": "48cec20f-b029-3704-b70f-a70477146e51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "junger Mann, der sich schlecht oder unhöflich benimmt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "figurative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ddd4f79f-26fb-4faa-839d-a144ccf78beb",
                                                "sense_id": "2e78ee83-3170-385b-855c-f7d285caa0a5",
                                                "text": "Benimm dich nicht wie ein Flegel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36f94e43-c032-4e45-9e9e-429f19e85cb1",
                                                "sense_id": "2e78ee83-3170-385b-855c-f7d285caa0a5",
                                                "text": "„Der Flegel schlug einen herrischen Ton an und wollte wissen, was ich damit gemacht hätte; darauf gab ich ihm zur Antwort, ich hätte ihm keine Rechenschaft abzulegen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74d18ff0-69b4-49c7-9f4b-86fb3acbc8ef",
                                                "sense_id": "2e78ee83-3170-385b-855c-f7d285caa0a5",
                                                "text": "„Goethe und Carl August konnten auch ungehobelte Flegel sein, und Wieland hat Mühe, seine Gelassenheit zu bewahren.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a4e6626-dcc7-3a32-aed0-b178b7fc1181",
                                        "entry_id": "48cec20f-b029-3704-b70f-a70477146e51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "bäuerliches Handgerät mit einem Stiel und einer Keule zum Trennen (Dreschen) der Getreidekörner vom Stroh"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32e4510e-3b21-4f7e-acdd-fe2dd6225a4c",
                                                "sense_id": "6a4e6626-dcc7-3a32-aed0-b178b7fc1181",
                                                "text": "Das dreschen mit dem Flegel war härteste körperliche Arbeit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dc230e0e-95ed-484f-81b6-edbce84c7c7a",
                                                "sense_id": "6a4e6626-dcc7-3a32-aed0-b178b7fc1181",
                                                "text": "„Winter ists wieder, und der Großvater stutzt einen abgelegten Flegel der Anderthalbmeter-Großmutter für mich.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a3b2e745-2f7e-365a-b974-2eed99f7c11d",
                                        "entry_id": "48cec20f-b029-3704-b70f-a70477146e51",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Schlagwaffe, die im Mittelalter gebraucht wurde"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7da3177-4cdb-4b32-abe1-c2607b1b2ed7",
                                                "sense_id": "a3b2e745-2f7e-365a-b974-2eed99f7c11d",
                                                "text": "Der Flegel wird häufig mit dem Morgenstern verwechselt, der jedoch keine Kette besaß."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
